{
  "id": "DrugBank_DB00694 - MONDO_18437",
  "verbalization": "Daunorubicin is implicated in the treatment of Acute Myeloid Leukemia (AML) with Npm1 somatic mutations through a mechanism involving the drug's interaction with Glasdegib. The evidence suggests that Daunorubicin, through its indication for Acute Myeloblastic Leukemia With Maturation and Acute Myeloblastic Leukemia Without Maturation, leads to the activation of Glasdegib, which in turn targets AML with Npm1 mutations. This pathway is consistent across multiple paths, indicating a general role of Glasdegib in the pathogenesis of this leukemia subtype. The presence of a common downstream target, AML with Npm1 mutations, supports the notion that Glasdegib acts as a mediator in the drug's therapeutic effect. The integration of these pathways highlights a potential mechanism by which Daunorubicin may influence the development or progression of AML with Npm1 mutations, though further experimental validation is needed to confirm the direct causal relationship.",
